From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: qcom: also check the xHCI root hub before reading the port speed

Follow-up to 0117. __usb_create_hcd() sets the xHCI platform device's driver
data before usb_add_hcd() has allocated and registered the root hub, and
usb_hub_find_child() dereferences the root hub (hdev->maxchild). A glue
suspend in that window would oops like the NULL hcd did. Report an unknown
speed then, as for a missing hcd. Suggested by GPT-6.1-Sol while reviewing
0117; it does not make a concurrent xHCI removal safe (that still relies on
stable roles and PM ordering during suspend).

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom-legacy.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom-legacy.c
@@ -330,8 +330,10 @@
 	/*
 	 * The xHCI platform device outlives its driver: with xhci-hcd unbound
 	 * (sysfs unbind) there is no hcd, and system suspend used to oops here.
+	 * __usb_create_hcd() also sets the driver data before usb_add_hcd() has
+	 * registered the root hub, and usb_hub_find_child() dereferences it.
 	 */
-	if (!hcd)
+	if (!hcd || !hcd->self.root_hub)
 		return USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -242,8 +242,10 @@
 	/*
 	 * The xHCI platform device outlives its driver: with xhci-hcd unbound
 	 * (sysfs unbind) there is no hcd, and system suspend used to oops here.
+	 * __usb_create_hcd() also sets the driver data before usb_add_hcd() has
+	 * registered the root hub, and usb_hub_find_child() dereferences it.
 	 */
-	if (!hcd)
+	if (!hcd || !hcd->self.root_hub)
 		return USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB
